From: captain <captain@lcars.local>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:54:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] Pinefeat CEF: refresh the state once a second

TimerHit() refreshes the state only once a second has passed since
lastUpdate, but lastUpdate was set only by the constructor and by
CALIBRATE. A second after either, the test held at every pass of the
timer, every 50 ms with the default polling period: `e` twenty times a
second, and, while the focuser is still, `e f r d a`, a hundred commands
a second.

lastUpdate is now set at each refresh: `e`, and while still `e f r d a`,
once a second. CALIBRATE keeps its delay.
---
 drivers/focuser/pinefeat_cef.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/focuser/pinefeat_cef.cpp b/drivers/focuser/pinefeat_cef.cpp
index b335f09..afdb1dc 100644
--- a/drivers/focuser/pinefeat_cef.cpp
+++ b/drivers/focuser/pinefeat_cef.cpp
@@ -473,6 +473,10 @@ void PinefeatCEF::TimerHit()
     auto now = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
     auto elapsed = std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::seconds>(now - lastUpdate).count();
 
+    // Once a second: the next refresh is a second after this one
+    if (elapsed >= 1)
+        lastUpdate = now;
+
     if (elapsed >= 1 && isNotMoving())
     {
         int32_t pos, max;
